From 5abcef493edce8da0d23c1d0a735dc6db064a686 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Matthieu <matthieu.chanewenc@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 05:25:08 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Translate every built-in string (English, French) and support
 Next.js

- CoreloomI18nProvider (src/lib/i18n.tsx, @coreloom/i18n): labels,
  placeholders, screen-reader text and validation messages of every
  component and block come from one dictionary. English and French are
  built in; `messages` overrides single strings or adds a language;
  `dateLocale` drives Calendar and DatePicker. Props still win.
- Storybook gets a Language toolbar; the a11y tests also run in French.
- Next.js App Router verified end to end: blocks accept icons as
  elements (<HomeIcon />) as well as components, so a server component
  can render them.
- index.d.ts drops repeated local helper types.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Te9bARZBkSfcxCSZLhK4ZW
